  "answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions and leveraging AI for enhanced security, accessibility, and data visualization. The project is led by Marcus Cole, with key team members including Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). It received a $2M budget approval and a compliance budget increase to $55,000. Key milestones include a kickoff on July 15th, a call for ideas by July 20th, initial findings showing a potential 20% efficiency increase, the completion of the testing phase, and a celebration on October 10th. Upcoming activities include a meeting on August 5th to discuss findings and the start of the development phase next month under lead developer Omar Jensen."
